      "comments": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50438445",
      "image": null,
      "content": "Cloning entire Git repositories just to let an AI agent read or search a few files introduces massive disk and bandwidth overhead. When autonomous workflows query dozens of upstream dependencies, standard full clones quickly become an infrastructure bottleneck.\n\nExplorerepo solves this problem by speaking native Git protocol v2 over SSH or HTTPS using filtered fetches with tree:0 and blob:none filters. Instead of cloning gigabytes of historical data, the CLI executes operations like ripgrep, find, and cat directly against remote Git server endpoints using git-upload-pack.\n\nThe server transmits only the specific tree structures and blobs requested by the command. This cuts agent latency down to seconds and drops data transfer requirements by orders of magnitude on large codebases.\n\nOptimizing agent tool harnesses at the protocol level yields far better throughput than adding more compute."
    },
    {
