      "content": "Post-training quantization to ternary weights destroys model accuracy, but quantization-aware training from scratch preserves almost the entire floating-point baseline.\n\nA reproducible benchmark trained a 126 million parameter transformer across 503 million tokens on a single consumer RTX 4090 GPU in just 1.2 GPU hours. Evaluating BitNet b1.58 style ternary weights showed that naive post-training quantization caused an intolerable error increase of 0.66 bits per byte.\n\nQuantization-aware training closed that gap dramatically. The trained ternary model suffered only a 0.053 bits per byte degradation while slashing the deployed footprint from 252 megabytes down to 61 megabytes, representing a 76 percent size reduction.\n\nYou do not need a cluster of enterprise accelerators to experiment with radical weight compression."
