      "comments": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50442697",
      "image": null,
      "content": "Durable workflow engines promise seamless crash recovery by replaying execution histories. However, external side effects like credit card charges and email dispatch sit entirely outside the local durability perimeter.\n\nReplayGuard is a fault injection tool designed to test durable actors under node crashes, network timeouts, and dropped responses. In testing against real runtimes, it exposed subtle edge cases where workflows double-charge or silently skip external side effects during replay loops.\n\nBuilding reliable distributed workflows requires rigorous testing of non-deterministic boundaries. If you rely on durable execution primitives, do not assume replay safety until you verify external idempotency under simulated failure."
    },
    {
      "title": "Reviving JavaScript partial evaluation using AI agents and solvers",
