      "image": null,
      "content": "Concurrency integration tests against relational databases are notoriously unreliable because microsecond-level query execution masks real race conditions until production traffic hits.\n\nPg-interleave tackles this problem at the Postgres wire protocol layer. Sitting directly between your client application and the database server, it acts as a transparent proxy capable of freezing individual statements, delaying responses, abruptly severing connections post-commit, or explicitly injecting 40P01 deadlocks.\n\nIn standard concurrent read-modify-write benchmark tests without coordination, standard test suites reproduce lost updates only 0 to 5 times out of 100 runs. By introducing deterministic query scheduling and schedule fuzzing through the proxy, that reproduction rate jumps to 85 to 98 percent.\n\nYou do not need to alter application code to expose distributed concurrency bugs; you simply need precise control over protocol execution order."
